  "term": "REM behavior disorder",
  "definition": "REM behavior disorder is a sleep disorder in which a person shows vigorous, sometimes violent movements during REM sleep. The person may injure themselves or others, can be hard to wake, and often later remembers a vivid dream that matches the behavior.",
